    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Green. Here's what I implemented and why.\n\n## Change: age-band derived from `birthDate`\n\nThe request may now carry an ISO `birthDate`; the owner response reports `ageBand` (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) computed from that birth date against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\n**Files touched:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (date) to the `OwnerFields` request schema and `ageBand` (readOnly string) to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs are code-generated from this spec, so these give `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate` and `OwnerDto.ageBand` for free; MapStruct maps `birthDate` onto the entity by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field with a plain getter/setter (CC 1 each), mirroring the existing `registrationDate` column.\n\n3. **`AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small cohesive helper next to `ContactPreference`/`IdentityKey`: `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` \u2192 band, `null` when no birth date. As a fresh single-purpose class it carries no surrounding complexity.\n\n4. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 one line, `dto.setAgeBand(AgeBand.of(owner))`, following the existing pattern for `contactPreference`/`checkDigit` on the GET path (the path the test reads back through).\n\n5. **DB schemas/seeds** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to all four `schema.sql` files; hsqldb and mysql use positional seed inserts, so I appended a trailing `NULL` to each owners row (h2/postgres use column-list inserts and needed no seed change).\n\n## One pre-existing bug I had to fix\n\nThe test creates an owner **without a postcode**, which surfaced a latent NPE unrelated to age-band: `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` intentionally calls `Locality.of(null, postcode)` to derive region from postcode alone, but with a null postcode it falls through to `of(null)`, and `Map.of(...).getOrDefault(null, \u2026)` throws (immutable maps reject null keys). Create 500'd for any postcode-less owner. I guarded it in one line in `Locality.of(String)` (`null \u2192 \"UNKNOWN\"`), which is the intended semantics. Without this the new test's `createOwnerOk` couldn't succeed.\n\nI kept structural impact low by putting the new logic in a zero-context helper class and touching each existing method by a single line, rather than growing the mapper (whose accumulated complexity would have been the expensive place to add it).",
